              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "<B>Short description of the study</B><BR><BR>\nThis study involved the design and evaluation of a bronchoscopy simulation-based training course for intensivists in the Netherlands. The evaluation consisted of a questionnaire filled out by participants. This questionnaire contained closed-ended questions and open-ended questions. The full questionnaire will be published as a supplement to the article.<BR><BR>\n\n<B>Short description of the data files</B><BR><BR>\n-\tthe “Study 5 Bronchoscopy course intensivist” contains all open-ended questions and answers given by respondents. <BR><BR>\n-\tThe “Closed ended questions.sav” file contains all closed-ended questions and ratings given. Higher ratings equal more satisfaction.<BR><BR>\n\n<B>Parameter in .sav file - Open-ended question</B><BR><BR>\nPractice_time - I had sufficient time to practise<BR>\nMore_competent - The training made me feel more competent to perform future bronchoscopies<BR>\nGood_preparation - The training prepared me well for performing future bronchoscopies in the intensive care suite<BR>\nStandard_component\t- If an intensivist wishes to receive bronchoscopy training, part of this training should be simulation-based<BR>\nSatisfaction - On a scale of 1 to 5, how satisfied are you with the training?\nLearning_material_relevance - The reading materials offered were relevant<BR>\nPresentation_relevance - The content of the presentations was relevant<BR>\nPresentation_content - The content of the presentations was clear<BR>\nPresentation_clarity - The  presenting style of the presentations was clear <BR>\nVR_operation - Operating the bronchoscope of the VR simulator was realistic<BR>\nVR_anatomy - The anatomy depicted in the VR simulator was realistic<BR>\nVR_relevance - The VR simulator was relevant to learning to perform an inspection bronchoscopy<BR>\nModel_anatomy - The anatomy of the 3D bronchoscopy model was realistic<BR>\nModel_relevance - The 3D bronchoscopy model was relevant to learning to perform an inspection bronchoscopy<BR>\nTracheostoma_realistic - The simulated tracheostomy procedure was realistic<BR>\nTracheostoma_relevance - The simulated tracheostomy procedure was relevant to learning to perform a tracheostomy procedure under bronchoscopic guidance<BR>\nSkills - The training improved my bronchoscopy competences<BR>\nInspection - The training made me able to inspect all lobes and segments<BR>\nSupervision - I am satisfied with the supervision received<BR>\nSupervision_expertise - I am satisfied with the level of expertise of the instructors<BR><BR>"
                },
                "dsDescriptionDate": {
